2.34.1

The action_op_set_val(), preaction_op_set_val() and preop_op_set_val()
functions use chains of 'if (strcmp(...) == 0) ... else if (...)' to
match the user-supplied sysfs/preaction/preop string against the set of
valid options.

Replace each chain with a table-driven match_string() lookup that
pairs the option name with its corresponding WDOG_* value. This removes
the duplicated strcmp boilerplate and makes adding a new option a
single-line change to both the names and values arrays.

The preaction table preserves the existing #ifdef HAVE_DIE_NMI
conditional for the "pre_nmi" entry. match_string() internally uses
strcmp(), so the matching semantics are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Jiangshan Yi <yijiangshan@kylinos.cn>
